# Byte-exact reproduction across platforms.
#
# The genimages in-sync test (internal/cmd/genimages) reads the committed
# docs/images/*.svg files and byte-compares them against freshly generated,
# LF-terminated SVG output. Go example `// Output:` blocks are likewise compared
# against the source text. Git's autocrlf on the GitHub Windows CI runner would
# rewrite the LF-committed blobs to CRLF on checkout, so a golden .svg (or an
# example comment) would gain stray \r bytes and no longer match the library's
# LF output — a spurious CI failure on an otherwise-correct tree.
#
# `-text` disables ALL end-of-line conversion, so every checkout reproduces the
# committed blob EXACTLY on every platform without rewriting files.
* -text
